            <div xml:id="d431">

                <pb facs="0402" n="286" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg286"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 322.112G64.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Hartman to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Quito</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 4, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mr. Goo Kwai, an American citizen of Chinese birth, residing Hawaii and holding
                    passport issued by Department of State, numbered 34640, desires to enter Ecuador
                    to visit relatives. He was not permitted to land at Guayaquil except through the
                    good offices of the American Consulate which is responsible for his attitude
                    until the decision of the Foreign Office is made. I presented the case
                    informally to the Minister for Foreign Affairs on October 27 and again on
                    October 30, leaving memorandum with the Minister. To-day I received informal
                    memorandum from the Minister informing me that the President of Ecuador, not
                    wishing to establish a precedent which might produce complications in Ecuador in
                    the future, had determined not to decide the question without presenting it for
                    the consideration of the Secretary of State at Washington through the Ecuadorian
                    Legation. I will forward despatch with full details by next pouch.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hartman</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
